+```
+
+To fix this, flatten the list structure:
+
+```markdown
+- Item
+  - Nested item
+  - Nested item
+```
+
+A list's depth is the number of lists it is in, counting itself: a top-level
+list has depth 1. Ordered and unordered lists count alike; block quotes neither
+add to the depth nor reset it.
+
+Note: With the default value of `0` for `maximum`, there is no limit and this
+rule never reports a violation.
+
+Rationale: Deeply nested lists are hard to read and often better expressed as
+separate sections or tables.
+
